From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Knight <gallantcrusader@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [DEVELOPMENT PATCH 1/3] drm/asahi: hw: add RE-gated G15 and T6030
 scaffolding

Development only. This is scaffolding for a future M3 Pro (T6030)
bring-up, not GPU support. Everything here is under
CONFIG_DRM_ASAHI_G15_CANDIDATE, which the last patch of this series
adds; until then the code is compiled out.

Add GpuGen::G15 = 15, the gpu_gen that macOS GPUConfigurationVariable
reports on T6030. T6030 reports variant S, which GpuVariant already
has, so no new variant is needed. Add GpuCore::G15S for the G15X/G15S
class. Its firmware core type ID is unknown, so the discriminant is a
named RE-gated zero placeholder rather than an extrapolation of the
G13/G14 numbering.

Add hw/t603x.rs with HWCONFIG_T6030. Only the identity comes from the
device-derived silicon profile (macOS IORegistry on a Mac15,7): chip_id
0x6030, G15, variant S, two clusters (num_mgpus), and per cluster 10
cores, 10 frags and 4 GPs from 20/20/8 across the clusters.
Compile-time asserts tie those counts to the 0x1ff,0x1ff core masks and
18 active cores. num_dies = 1 is inferred instead: the pinned
t6030.dtsi has no die1 nodes, and the silicon profile has no die count.

Every other field is gated on reverse engineering: base clock, UAT OAS,
preemption buffer sizes, clustering metadata, tiling control,
HwConfigA/HwConfigB, HwDataShared1/2/3, firmware globals, sram_k,
unk_coef_a/b, the globals table, CS/AFR presence, temperature sensor
masks, firmware MMIO mappings and the SRAM window. Each is a named
RE_GATED_* constant holding zero or an empty table, labelled TODO(re),
so no nonzero value can pass for a tuned one. CS/AFR presence is a
bool, so it is a named fail-closed placeholder instead. No t600x, t602x
or t8112 value is copied.

No native validation. hardware_acceptance=false.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
